      "data": {
        "text": "**Begin Developing Code**\n\nI've started by reading the `detect_image_labels.py` file to understand the existing structure. Now, I'm ready to begin creating the required Python files for image and visual understanding tasks. I'll need to make sure that each \"scored\" file incorporates an external provider and contains identifiable information within the code to track the use of the external provider. Also, I must ensure the inclusion of helper utilities in their respective files.\n\n\n**Initiate File Planning**\n\nI've outlined the core files required, focusing on tasks like image description, text detection, and safety scoring, which I am planning for. I am using the Google Cloud Vision AI library and using the code read from `detect_image_labels.py` as a reference. I'm focusing on incorporating identifiable external provider use within each \"scored\" file.\n\n\n**Refine File Outlines**\n\nI've significantly refined the file structure and provider integrations. Now I'm clearly defining tasks for each, including `describe_image.py`, `detect_image_text.py`, and `score_image_safety.py`, all using Google Cloud Vision. Helper files for client configuration and model definitions, specifically `vision_client.py` and `vision_models.py`, are also planned. I'm noting later steps that include generative AI tasks for summarization and translation, and text-based safety validation.\n\n\n**Begin File Mapping**\n\nI've carefully mapped out all the required files, considering both immediate and future development. I have a firm understanding of the existing integration demonstrated in `detect_image_labels.py`. Now, I'm ready to begin creating the core files. My plan is to start with the ones that support the image understanding tasks, then move on to the helper files.\n\n\n",
